Since the job only runs monthly
This is actually the most important insight: since it's a monthly job (not daily), and INACTIVE_ACCOUNT_TIME was set to 30 days, this account was mathematically guaranteed to lock every single month — a 30-day gate on an account that's only used every ~30 days will occasionally tip over the threshold depending on exact day counts (28 vs 31-day months, leap years, etc.). Raising it to 90 gives comfortable headroom above the monthly cadence, so this shouldn't recur.
Summary for your ticket/documentation
Root cause: LGY_ANALYTICS (remote account via WEBLGY_OAR_DB db link) has INACTIVE_ACCOUNT_TIME = 30 days, but SRC_WEBLGY_DATAPUMP_JOB only connects monthly — a cadence too close to the threshold, causing intermittent auto-locks.
Fix applied: Raised INACTIVE_ACCOUNT_TIME to 90 days on the remote profile.
Verification: Job ran successfully 3 times on 9/1/2026 after the fix, including two runs after the profile change.
